  "requirements": [
    {
      "id": "R1",
      "summary": "pass-through — A result whose measured bytes are ≤ `delivery_ceiling_bytes` is delivered byte-identically to the pre-change SDK marshaling."
    },
    {
      "id": "R2",
      "summary": "measurement — The measure is the byte length of the SDK-marshaled complete `mcp.CallToolResult`; every occurrence in the serialized form counts; no deduplication, reordering, or pretty-printing may reduce it"
    },
    {
      "id": "R3",
      "summary": "preview — An over-ceiling retainable result is delivered on every paged surface (call_tool, directly invoked projected tools, search_tools, describe_tool) as a preview ≤ `preview_ceiling_bytes` whose `Content` is a non-empty UTF-8"
    },
    {
      "id": "R4",
      "summary": "handles — Handles are opaque `crypto/rand` values (43-char base64url), bound to one owner namespace (session + admitted epoch, or the session-less publisher namespace), and expire at `handle_ttl`"
    },
    {
      "id": "R5",
      "summary": "paging completeness — Each page is a rune-aligned valid-UTF-8 slice of the serialized retained bytes (cut points fall only on rune boundaries; SDK JSON marshaling is valid UTF-8), so concatenating all pages of a handle reproduces the retained"
    },
    {
      "id": "R6",
      "summary": "bounded retention — Retention is hard-bounded per namespace in bytes and entries, capped per entry by `max_retained_result_bytes`, and evicts FIFO / expires by TTL under those bounds"
    },
    {
      "id": "R7",
      "summary": "retired namespace — Namespace retirement leaves a store-internal tombstone with a stated lifetime (`tombstone_ttl`) and an explicit clearing condition, counted in retention accounting; wire-level retrieval of a handle from a retired namespa"
    },
    {
      "id": "R8",
      "summary": "execution facts — `is_error` and `upstream_code` are preserved identically on the preview, every page, and every terminal; paging never re-executes the upstream; bridge-side dispatch failures remain small `errorResult` responses, never pa"
    },
    {
      "id": "R9",
      "summary": "pinning — The per-entry `upstream_code` bound and rendered value, and the page/preview sizing derived from the ceilings, are fixed at retention time; a config reload of `max_upstream_code_bytes`, `delivery_ceiling_bytes` or `previ"
    },
    {
      "id": "R10",
      "summary": "terminals — Each unretainable over-ceiling outcome — per-entry cap exceeded, aggregate cap exceeded, namespace retired before commit, entropy failure at handle generation — produces a distinct typed terminal preview (no handle), bou"
    },
    {
      "id": "R11",
      "summary": "config validation — All documented relations are validated at config load with typed diagnostics; startup fails closed: (a) `preview_ceiling_bytes < delivery_ceiling_bytes`, equal rejected; (b) `max_retained_result_bytes > delivery_ceiling_"
    },
    {
      "id": "R12",
      "summary": "finite labels — Log labels `{operation}` and `{outcome}` take values only from declared enumerations; an unlisted value fails the vocabulary test; every enumerated value has at least one producing path."
    },
    {
      "id": "R13",
      "summary": "retrieval input contract — `retrieve_result` validates its input handler-side, never relying on a JSON-schema pattern for this built-in surface: a shape-invalid handle or page returns `invalid_arguments`, and a page beyond the entry's `total_pages"
    },
    {
      "id": "R14",
      "summary": "terminal field semantics — A terminal's `StructuredContent` carries `retention`, whose allowed values are exactly the four terminal codes {`result_capacity_exceeded`, `result_aggregate_capacity_exceeded`, `result_namespace_retired`, `result_entrop"
    },
    {
      "id": "R15",
      "summary": "documentation — README and the `retrieve_result` tool description document the handle/page retrieval contract (handle, page, `total_pages`, bounded preview, byte-exact page concatenation) and replace the \"complete upstream CallToolResul"
    },
    {
      "id": "R16",
      "summary": "sweep markers — Expiry and eviction install store-internal markers parallel to the tombstone: stated lifetime (`tombstone_ttl`), explicit clearing condition — cleared when the sweep observes marker age > lifetime — counted in `max_bytes"
    }
  ],
